comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T05:01:25.983Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: full all-status corpus, live pm-bj7rq0 and closed pm-ckb8w5 metadata/history lineage, request-specific search and refreshed open/in-progress inventories. The predecessor shipped other named corpus and policy keepers and remains completed. This exact omitted context-decision file is a new scoped child, required by the current SDK continuation delivery; no timeout retry threshold or source denominator change is authorized."
  "2026-10-21T05:05:19.658Z","harness:codex","Independent keeper fails before allocation: contracts.exclude omits the context-decision path. The unchanged contextual suite already passed7 focused cases with the final SDK declarations before this scheduling change. Add the complete four-test file to the existing serial group exactly once, preserve deadlines and source populations, and retain the first full-suite timeout as failed evidence."
  "2026-10-21T05:06:42.911Z","harness:codex","After allocation, the complete keeper/context command passes6 tests across2 files. The membership negative control failed before the config change; no source assertion,200-item population,30000ms completion deadline, hook deadline or retry policy changed. Complete final-source coverage remains required before closure."
  "2026-10-21T05:41:34.584Z","harness:codex","The independent membership keeper fails before allocation and passes after it. All 6 linked keeper/context tests pass, and complete accepted source coverage passes 10922 tests with 3 configured skips and exact 100/100/100/100. The original context timeout and separate transport-benchmark timeout remain failed historical receipts rather than erased evidence."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T05:07:55.836Z","harness:codex","A real corpus fixture can need serial allocation even when its surrounding suite is not named performance. Prove cohort membership independently and preserve population, assertions, deadlines, retry policy and the full coverage denominator."
